    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c2ca5a01-dab1-3fec-8b9b-710fafa497aa",
                "word": "usurious",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0a6ac838-e4f1-4923-ac52-b2fc003b0211",
                        "entry_id": "c2ca5a01-dab1-3fec-8b9b-710fafa497aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more usurious"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "a111bae9-0c37-4248-9823-164ebdbbfe7c",
                        "entry_id": "c2ca5a01-dab1-3fec-8b9b-710fafa497aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most usurious"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6304755e-986f-3f85-9bf3-2a88d29c1e67",
                        "entry_id": "c2ca5a01-dab1-3fec-8b9b-710fafa497aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to usury."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e443d4dc-749f-460a-9875-02704b39b18d",
                                "sense_id": "6304755e-986f-3f85-9bf3-2a88d29c1e67",
                                "text": "If an Executor pay an Uſurious Bond, other Creditors may make a Devaſtavit of it, Hob. p. 167. If a Man be bound in an Obligation Uſurious, the Bond is void between the Parties, yea and Strangers ſhall take the advantage of it; and therefore if ſuch an Obligor makes his Executor and die, and the Executor pay the uſurious Bond, other Creditors may ſhew it, and make a Devaſtavit of it, in Winchcomb and the Biſhop of Wincheſter’s Caſe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13e6313f-ce51-40df-bd47-e7a33d597abb",
                                "sense_id": "6304755e-986f-3f85-9bf3-2a88d29c1e67",
                                "text": "The fallacy of his [Justice William Best’s] argument is, that he supposes the objection to the plaintiff’s recovery to be, that his contract with the defendant is usurious; whereas the objection really arises from the circumstance that these notes are deposited to enforce another contract, which was usurious, and the defence rests on this — not that more than 5 per cent. is reserved by these bills, but that they are destined to enforce a contract which is usurious."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bcd13bc7-2e88-4ff9-a5b2-c2b6178cc3ab",
                                "sense_id": "6304755e-986f-3f85-9bf3-2a88d29c1e67",
                                "text": "Behold the name given by Christ to both the usurer and his usurious borrower. Sinners lend to sinners; each is a sinner, the usurer and the borrower."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a02dd401-38ee-42c8-aa7f-dabebcbbd1e2",
                                "sense_id": "6304755e-986f-3f85-9bf3-2a88d29c1e67",
                                "text": "His one worldly care was to raise ready money; sufficient for the day is the evil thereof. And how he raised it: From usurious insatiable Jews; every fresh Jew sticking on him like a fresh horseleech, sucking his and our life out; crying continually, Give! give!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a87b660-3a81-4938-b1a2-1ef59e1b7909",
                                "sense_id": "6304755e-986f-3f85-9bf3-2a88d29c1e67",
                                "text": "The originator of a usurious loan in California is subject to severe civil penalties."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "812280cb-686d-3430-ada8-40b9620822a8",
                        "entry_id": "c2ca5a01-dab1-3fec-8b9b-710fafa497aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Exorbitant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "abb0cdd9-eda9-4e5c-a37e-f07acf68bf76",
                                "sense_id": "812280cb-686d-3430-ada8-40b9620822a8",
                                "text": "But nature, violated by these excesses, exacts a most usurious interest for this illicit indulgence. She makes them pay for moments of rapture with hours of despair."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2be1d509-f1a1-42d7-98ed-0d09ce3209cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "c2ca5a01-dab1-3fec-8b9b-710fafa497aa",
                        "source_sense_description": "Of or pertaining to usury",
                        "target_lang_word": "usuraire",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "usuraire",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b50521c-4d17-3270-b423-92b6826ba8b6",
                                        "entry_id": "3d925b79-2b5c-34db-be5f-b13f634e6451",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Où il y a manifestement de l’usure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95f914c7-c8de-448c-8cc3-21bb71bb3e11",
                                                "sense_id": "7b50521c-4d17-3270-b423-92b6826ba8b6",
                                                "text": "L’officier entreprit de faire une distinction entre les créanciers de l’état, d’exclure du droit absolu à la bonne foi du gouvernement ceux qui avaient prêté à un taux trop élevé, à un taux usuraire ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65a4d853-5dd1-4cdd-8b01-c973c5d50215",
                                                "sense_id": "7b50521c-4d17-3270-b423-92b6826ba8b6",
                                                "text": "Il ne refusait jamais d'accéder aux demandes de petits prêts d'argent qu'il consentait à des taux point trop usuraires pour l'époque."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44c01a5e-32f5-4db7-93fc-4de390a926bf",
                                                "sense_id": "7b50521c-4d17-3270-b423-92b6826ba8b6",
                                                "text": "Aux cultivateurs de la région, il prêtait sur hypothèques, comme pour leur rendre service et avec une bonhomie qui faisait oublier, sur le moment, ses taux usuraires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d75cbe14-f5f4-4081-a6f8-08a266fcb747",
                                                "sense_id": "7b50521c-4d17-3270-b423-92b6826ba8b6",
                                                "text": "– Huit pour cent ! Ça va bien. Je veux bien laisser Courtois répéter à tout bout de champ que ce n’est pas usuraire. C’est, en tout cas, terriblement lourd et, je peux le dire, entre nous, à la limite de l’honnêteté."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "286edf44-8108-4f2b-8630-0d0378322eb1",
                                                "sense_id": "7b50521c-4d17-3270-b423-92b6826ba8b6",
                                                "text": "Les serfs qui ne pouvaient payer les taxes exigées s’endettaient, souvent à des taux usuraires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4fa6bed-3ecc-44a7-ab4b-07d29bf3865a",
                                                "sense_id": "7b50521c-4d17-3270-b423-92b6826ba8b6",
                                                "text": "Aux entreprises, il demande d’autre part de ne pas réclamer de « compensations usuraires » liées à ces arrêts de chantier pour cas de force majeure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
